---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const download = '/downloads/MIDI%20Pass%20Lowest%20Note%20Only%20v1.amxd';
---

<Base
	title="MIDI Pass Lowest Note Only — Enoki Solutions"
	description="MIDI Pass Lowest Note Only is a free Max for Live MIDI effect for Ableton Live that passes only the lowest held note and can strip keyswitches."
>
	<section class="product">
		<div class="product-intro">
			<p class="kicker">Max for Live device</p>
			<h2>MIDI Pass Lowest Note Only</h2>
			<p class="product-lede">
				A small MIDI effect for Ableton Live that turns any polyphonic
				MIDI — wherever notes overlap — into a single line by passing
				only the lowest held note — with optional
				keyswitch stripping.
			</p>
		</div>

		<ul class="features">
			<li>
				<h3>Built for pitch-following plugins</h3>
				<p>
					Made to feed MIDI into <a
						href="https://www.aeonslight.com/plugins/eq">Aeons Light EQ</a>, which can follow MIDI notes. Put the device on the
					track playing the part, followed by Ableton's External
					Instrument device with its MIDI output routed to the EQ — no
					separate MIDI track to keep in sync when the part changes.
				</p>
				<p>
					Add Ableton's Pitch device set to −12 st before the External
					Instrument. There's no agreed standard for whether MIDI note
					60 is C3, C4, or C5, and Live and the EQ number octaves one
					apart, so without the offset the EQ tracks an octave high.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<h3>Lowest note only</h3>
				<p>
					When on, only the lowest held note is output, making any
					part monophonic. Handy for driving a bass line or mono synth
					from any polyphonic part.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<h3>Strip keyswitches</h3>
				<p>
					Notes below Keyswitch Low (default C1) or above Keyswitch
					High (default F6) are treated as keyswitches and removed,
					so articulation changes don't reach the instrument.
				</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<h3>Pass-through when off</h3>
				<p>
					With both buttons off, the device passes all MIDI through
					untouched.
				</p>
			</li>
		</ul>

		<div class="cta">
			<p class="cta-status">Free download, version 1. Requires Ableton Live 12.4.5 or later with Max for Live (Max 9).</p>
			<div class="cta-buttons">
				<a class="button button-primary" href={download} download
					>Download v1 (.amxd)</a
				>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
